WEBVTT

00:07.500 --> 00:12.260
Hi, all. I'm still here
and still doing great.

00:13.470 --> 00:16.220
I've finally finished the
lyrics to our new song!

00:17.760 --> 00:21.229
Also, the owner of SuperNova,
where Suzu works part time,

00:21.230 --> 00:28.820
was kind enough to let us rehearse there after
hours to prepare for our upcoming regular show.

00:29.480 --> 00:33.645
I want to do my absolute best, to give you
all even more rock-and-roll power than before!

00:33.646 --> 00:35.390
Closed early today. Come again soon, okay?

00:39.450 --> 00:40.580
Excuse me.

00:40.950 --> 00:41.950
Huh?

00:42.460 --> 00:46.329
Sonico, what are you doing
here? We're closed now.

00:46.330 --> 00:50.920
Ah, Miina! Hi there. Um, well...

00:52.300 --> 00:55.679
First Astronomical Velocity is going
to rehearse for our live show.

00:55.680 --> 00:57.679
A r-rehearsal?

00:57.680 --> 00:59.140
Yes, that's right.

00:59.770 --> 01:06.099
Thank you very much, Ma'am. I'm sorry for
such a sudden request, and at this hour...

01:06.100 --> 01:10.609
It's fine. But in return, I look forward
to a stellar live performance.

01:10.610 --> 01:11.610
Right!

01:11.940 --> 01:15.240
We'll do our best to live
up to your expectations!

01:15.610 --> 01:20.200
Um, Nico, I haven't finished cleaning yet.
Have a seat in the waiting room.

01:20.790 --> 01:22.540
Fuuri will be here soon.

01:22.870 --> 01:25.040
Okay, understood!

02:03.160 --> 02:09.839
Sorry I'm late. The reason I'm late is, without a
doubt, that the line at the meat bun vendor was so...

02:09.840 --> 02:11.879
Sonico! Sonico!

02:11.880 --> 02:14.009
Huh? What's the matter?

02:14.010 --> 02:19.139
Oh, Fuuri! Sonico's in the waiting
room and won't come out.

02:19.140 --> 02:19.680
She won't?

02:19.680 --> 02:20.600
Sonico! Sonico!
She won't?

02:20.601 --> 02:21.850
Sonico! Sonico!

02:22.430 --> 02:24.720
Miina, I brought the owner.

02:24.980 --> 02:25.980
The key!

02:26.310 --> 02:27.310
Here.

02:42.700 --> 02:43.700
Ni...

02:44.490 --> 02:45.750
Nico?!

02:49.370 --> 02:50.879
Ippai hibiki MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:50.880 --> 02:52.379
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:52.380 --> 02:53.879
Ippai todoke FEELING
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:53.880 --> 02:55.379
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

02:55.380 --> 02:56.839
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:56.840 --> 02:58.356
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:58.380 --> 02:59.969
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:59.970 --> 03:02.220
Super Soni LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

03:14.190 --> 03:18.650
Saikin omoitsukimashita
Lately, I've come to realize

03:20.280 --> 03:24.620
Kimochi tsutaeru tte taihen
That getting feelings across is tough

03:26.370 --> 03:31.169
Umaku dekitari dekinattari
Whether it goes well or not

03:31.170 --> 03:34.919
Muzukashii kara oku no te de
Is tough, so my trump card

03:34.920 --> 03:37.510
Mouretsu taiatari desu
Is going for it at full force

03:39.260 --> 03:41.550
Dakedo hitomishiri (hitomishiri)
But I'm shy (shy)

03:42.180 --> 03:44.980
Gomakashite senobi (senobi)
I act like it's nothing and aim high (high)

03:45.350 --> 03:46.889
Ashi ga gakuburu de
With legs trembling

03:46.890 --> 03:50.140
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

03:50.520 --> 03:53.149
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

03:53.150 --> 03:56.190
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

03:56.520 --> 03:59.189
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

03:59.190 --> 04:02.739
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

04:02.740 --> 04:04.256
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

04:04.280 --> 04:05.699
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

04:05.700 --> 04:07.346
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

04:07.370 --> 04:08.619
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

04:08.620 --> 04:10.289
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

04:10.290 --> 04:11.619
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

04:11.620 --> 04:13.436
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

04:13.460 --> 04:15.630
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

04:19.970 --> 04:22.840
Suzu. Fuuri.

04:23.680 --> 04:27.390
I wanted to rock with you forever.

04:28.220 --> 04:36.220
I'm not all that, but I'll do my best, so
together... the three of us... Let's always rock.

04:41.700 --> 04:43.820
N-Nico...

04:44.110 --> 04:45.280
Nico!

04:45.570 --> 04:46.870
NICO!

04:47.950 --> 04:49.290
Nico!

04:57.960 --> 05:00.920
Looks like she slipped
and knocked herself out.

05:01.970 --> 05:04.610
Tomato Juice

05:02.510 --> 05:04.630
Plus, there's a plastic
drink bottle there...

05:06.850 --> 05:09.310
And tracks where she slipped.

05:14.020 --> 05:17.809
I swear. Nico had us worrying over nothing!

05:17.810 --> 05:20.819
Still, it's good that she
wasn't seriously hurt.

05:20.820 --> 05:23.240
Yes. That's the silver lining in this!

05:23.490 --> 05:26.029
But now we can't have our rehearsal.

05:26.030 --> 05:27.030
No!

05:27.280 --> 05:28.280
This...

05:31.330 --> 05:33.540
This is a CASE!

05:35.460 --> 05:37.039
Uh, Ena?

05:37.040 --> 05:38.040
"Ena"?

05:38.170 --> 05:39.919
Wh-who is she?

05:39.920 --> 05:46.050
My little sister, Ena. She thinks she's a
detective and sticks her nose into everything.

05:47.220 --> 05:48.970
What are you doing here?

05:49.350 --> 05:55.850
Well, I smelled a case brewing, of course! Such is
the intuition of the great detective Ena Fujimi!

05:56.190 --> 05:58.710
If intuition brought you here,
then you didn't "smell" anything!

06:00.730 --> 06:02.730
So then, Sonico was found collapsed.

06:03.230 --> 06:04.489
In a locked room...

06:04.490 --> 06:06.150
How do you know it was locked?!

06:06.360 --> 06:07.859
This is definitely a case.

06:07.860 --> 06:12.370
Um, Ena? Nico just slipped
and knocked herself out.

06:12.700 --> 06:14.750
What makes you so sure?

06:15.460 --> 06:18.209
There are marks on the
floor where she slipped.

06:18.210 --> 06:20.669
That's what makes this a case!

06:20.670 --> 06:21.920
How do you figure?

06:22.500 --> 06:27.090
It's been made to look like an
accident to cover up the real crime.

06:27.550 --> 06:29.890
I will reveal what actually happened.

06:30.930 --> 06:35.600
One truth prevails! In the name of
the great detective Ena Fujimi!

06:39.850 --> 06:41.480
Nico just won't wake up, huh?

06:41.770 --> 06:43.569
She still hasn't woken up.

06:43.570 --> 06:46.360
Hey! Don't ignore me!

06:46.950 --> 06:50.489
Suzu, why don't we humor Ena for now? It looks like it'll
be a while before Nico wakes up. C'mon! You're being mean!

06:50.490 --> 06:54.050
Suzu, why don't we humor Ena for now? It looks
like it'll be a while before Nico wakes up.

06:54.240 --> 07:00.380
I guess you're right. Tell us then, O
great Ena. What is this deduction of yours?

07:01.290 --> 07:04.549
I'm not entirely sure I'm
NOT being made fun of...

07:04.550 --> 07:09.130
In any case! I'll hear your alibis for
the time of this incident.

07:12.680 --> 07:17.270
I was cleaning the toilets when Nico
was in the waiting room.

07:17.850 --> 07:21.230
I was cleaning the stage.

07:22.020 --> 07:25.730
I was at the register,
doing the daily receipts.

07:26.150 --> 07:30.610
I was late because I was
in line buying a meat bun.

07:30.820 --> 07:38.820
The waiting room door was locked when I got here, and
when Miina opened it, Nico was lying there on the floor!

07:41.120 --> 07:42.830
I see. I've solved it.

07:43.130 --> 07:44.130
Huh?!

07:44.210 --> 07:45.960
The culprit in this case is...

07:47.920 --> 07:49.760
YOU, Miina!

07:53.260 --> 07:57.810
Miina, who works part time here at
SuperNova, was seriously hurting for money.

07:58.930 --> 08:04.270
When she saw the owner counting the
day's receipts, evil probably overcame her!

08:05.320 --> 08:10.400
In a fit, Miina nearly attacked the owner
to steal the profits. But then!

08:11.070 --> 08:14.529
Sonico happened to spy
her from the waiting room.

08:14.530 --> 08:15.950
Staaaare.

08:17.120 --> 08:21.829
Miina aborted her crime and casually
approached the waiting room.

08:21.830 --> 08:24.710
She aimed for the door and... BOOM!

08:25.710 --> 08:30.220
The powerful blow sent Sonico stumbling
back. She slipped on the bottle...

08:34.590 --> 08:35.970
And lost consciousness.

08:36.890 --> 08:38.720
That is the truth of this case.

08:39.220 --> 08:41.890
Your theory is a total mess.

08:42.190 --> 08:46.270
I never attacked the owner.
And I have no money troubles.

08:47.940 --> 08:53.320
The proof is this cell phone. I took the
liberty of borrowing it from Miina's locker.

08:53.860 --> 08:54.820
When?

08:54.821 --> 08:57.409
Upon examining it, I learned the truth.

08:57.410 --> 08:58.410
Again, when?!

08:58.411 --> 09:00.080
O-on this phone...

09:01.200 --> 09:06.209
One can find several online purchases. Hence
the reason she DOES have money troubles!

09:06.210 --> 09:09.209
Um, Ena? That's MY phone.

09:09.210 --> 09:10.210
Huh?!

09:10.300 --> 09:13.300
Also, Miina comes from
a very wealthy family.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.220
Really?

09:18.140 --> 09:20.639
So the true culprit
makes her fatal mistake.

09:20.640 --> 09:21.640
HUH?

09:21.770 --> 09:27.400
That "theory" just now was a trap set to draw
her out. The one really behind this case...

09:28.150 --> 09:29.900
is YOU, Suzu!

09:30.280 --> 09:32.110
How do you figure that?!

09:32.690 --> 09:36.820
As I learned from your phone,
you are hurting for money.

09:39.120 --> 09:43.000
That's more than enough motive for
going after the profits. But!

09:44.120 --> 09:45.209
When Sonico spotted you...

09:45.210 --> 09:46.770
Staaaaaare...
When Sonico spotted you...

09:47.250 --> 09:50.840
you smashed down the door with your
patented Atmospheric Entry Drop Kick!

09:55.050 --> 09:57.680
Whereupon Sonico... yada yada yada.

09:58.680 --> 10:01.350
THAT is the truth of this case.

10:01.970 --> 10:09.019
Question! If your theory is true then why,
pray tell, was the waiting room door locked?

10:09.020 --> 10:12.940
I have the only key. There are no spares.

10:13.990 --> 10:17.660
It seems you've completely
fallen for my two-tiered trap!

10:17.990 --> 10:19.490
What do you mean?

10:19.990 --> 10:25.410
As the owner herself just said, she is the
only one with a waiting-room key.

10:25.960 --> 10:30.170
Therefore, she was the only one who
could have locked the door!

10:30.460 --> 10:33.960
You saying I'M the
culprit? What's my motive?

10:34.590 --> 10:36.920
The stage rental fee.

10:37.510 --> 10:43.350
While the others were cleaning up, you and Sonico
had an argument about the stage rental fee.

10:43.490 --> 10:45.740
MONEY!!

10:43.850 --> 10:45.850
The owner wanted more money.

10:46.100 --> 10:48.290
NO!!

10:46.480 --> 10:48.310
But Sonico refused to pay!

10:48.980 --> 10:52.980
Sonico's stubborn refusal filled the
owner with murderous rage!

10:53.900 --> 10:57.450
And so, she tried using her supple
breasts to crush Sonico to death!

10:57.860 --> 11:00.280
But Sonico, possessing
her own ample bosom...

11:01.200 --> 11:03.490
launched a fierce counterattack!

11:06.660 --> 11:09.000
The battle raged on,
with no clear end in sight.

11:12.750 --> 11:14.710
Until, at last, Sonico was defeated!

11:16.300 --> 11:20.930
After making it look like Sonico had
tripped, the owner left the waiting room...

11:21.510 --> 11:24.760
Not forgetting, of
course, to lock the door.

11:26.390 --> 11:30.229
Then, she casually began
work on the day's receipts,

11:30.230 --> 11:35.230
playing along when things came to light
to avoid suspicion as the real culprit.

11:35.940 --> 11:39.279
Well? That's the truth of
this locked-room mystery.

11:39.280 --> 11:40.660
No, it's not!

11:41.530 --> 11:47.449
We weren't paying a stage rental fee.
We had it for free! She gave it to us!

11:47.450 --> 11:48.450
Huh?

11:50.710 --> 11:51.829
Nico?!

11:51.830 --> 11:52.830
Nico!

11:53.000 --> 11:58.970
You awake? Then hurry up and set Ena straight!
Tell her you just slipped and passed out.

11:59.380 --> 12:01.840
That's not true! This is a case.

12:02.220 --> 12:06.009
Sonico, don't get up.
Sleeeep. That's a good girl!

12:06.010 --> 12:08.100
Why are you trying to keep her asleep?!

12:08.890 --> 12:12.150
Well, if she wakes up,
she'll tell us what happened.

12:12.440 --> 12:13.600
I won't get to deduce it!

12:13.730 --> 12:16.440
Ena, you dummy! We
don't need to "deduce" it!

12:17.650 --> 12:18.570
Nico!

12:18.571 --> 12:20.610
My... guitar...

12:21.490 --> 12:22.610
"Guitar"?

12:27.450 --> 12:30.039
Nico's guitar is gone.

12:30.040 --> 12:31.790
So that could mean...

12:32.210 --> 12:33.920
She DIDN'T slip.

12:34.500 --> 12:37.500
She was attacked by
someone who wanted her guitar.

12:37.920 --> 12:38.920
As I thought.

12:38.960 --> 12:40.800
This is a case!

12:53.440 --> 12:55.100
It's not in her locker, either.

12:55.350 --> 13:01.989
Her wallet's untouched. So the culprit
wasn't after her valuables. Just her guitar.

13:01.990 --> 13:04.199
But this room was locked.

13:04.200 --> 13:06.740
Y-yes, it was definitely locked.

13:07.240 --> 13:09.239
This is the only key.

13:09.240 --> 13:12.370
There are no spares and I don't
recall lending it to anyone.

13:13.080 --> 13:16.130
Then how did the culprit get in?

13:16.830 --> 13:19.500
There's not a room on
Earth that can't be broken into.

13:20.630 --> 13:23.340
And the way the culprit
entered this locked room...

13:24.590 --> 13:25.760
is THAT!

13:27.090 --> 13:28.549
The air duct?

13:28.550 --> 13:31.470
How could someone fit
in something that small?!

13:32.100 --> 13:33.850
Who said it was a person inside?

13:34.060 --> 13:35.389
What do you mean?

13:35.390 --> 13:36.940
I believe that the culprit...

13:37.730 --> 13:39.230
used a robot!

13:39.900 --> 13:41.230
A robot?!

13:42.190 --> 13:44.860
Yes. This is Akihabara,
the city of electronic brains!

13:45.360 --> 13:49.740
The culprit used a radio-controlled robot to
infiltrate the waiting room via the air duct.

13:51.290 --> 13:56.040
Without Sonico noticing, it jumped
up and unlocked the door...

13:56.750 --> 14:00.460
And then the culprit strode
in through the entrance.

14:02.960 --> 14:06.050
He attacked Sonico and stole her guitar.

14:07.130 --> 14:12.720
Afterward, he set the stage by using
the robot to relock the door...

14:14.140 --> 14:17.310
and sent it back through
the air duct. Well?

14:17.690 --> 14:21.230
That's the trick the culprit
used to enter the locked room.

14:21.650 --> 14:24.820
The robot got all the way back up there?

14:26.320 --> 14:28.490
That just wouldn't be possible.

14:28.870 --> 14:31.240
Well, then... I've got it!

14:31.830 --> 14:35.540
Though barely conscious,
Sonico tried to pursue the culprit.

14:35.910 --> 14:39.420
But just as she reached the door,
she lost consciousness.

14:40.040 --> 14:47.840
The force of her fall locked the door, and she
rolled all the way into the position we found her!

14:48.470 --> 14:50.680
There's no way that could've happened!

14:50.930 --> 14:53.060
Are you trying to shoot down my theories?!

14:53.510 --> 14:58.639
They're not theories! They're wild fantasies!
Fantasies! They're not worth taking seriously!

14:58.640 --> 15:06.190
The heck?! These are the theories of a
great detective! Fine, do as you like! Hmph!

15:06.780 --> 15:08.530
Now she's sulking.

15:09.240 --> 15:14.080
Just leave her be. Anyway, the truth
has to be way simpler.

15:14.540 --> 15:20.080
The culprit probably just knocked and Sonico let
him in. Then he attacked her and stole the guitar.

15:20.670 --> 15:24.550
I think we would've heard
Sonico cry out, in that case.

15:25.250 --> 15:29.010
Also, it doesn't explain
how the door was relocked.

15:29.340 --> 15:31.140
Th-that's true.

15:31.430 --> 15:36.270
Why would a thief be after
Nico's guitar in the first place?

15:36.560 --> 15:37.639
Do you think it was a
crazed fan of Sonico's?

15:37.640 --> 15:39.139
Sonico... A missing guitar... Their show... Rehearsal...
Do you think it was a crazed fan of Sonico's?

15:39.140 --> 15:42.780
Sonico... A missing guitar... Their show...
Rehearsal... Would a crazed fan hit her, though?

15:43.900 --> 15:48.900
Suzu! When did you decide
to hold rehearsal here today?!

15:49.280 --> 15:50.319
Enough with your theorie...

15:50.320 --> 15:51.610
Just tell me!

15:53.700 --> 15:59.250
This afternoon. I asked the owner, and she
said we could use the stage after closing.

15:59.710 --> 16:01.290
Who did you tell?

16:01.500 --> 16:04.290
I called Fuuri and Nico, of course.

16:04.750 --> 16:05.920
Anyone else?

16:07.550 --> 16:09.720
I... I didn't say anything!

16:10.300 --> 16:12.430
I didn't tell anyone, either.

16:12.930 --> 16:15.810
I didn't even know there
was going to be a rehearsal.

16:16.180 --> 16:21.810
What if Sonico told someone else
that you were rehearsing today?

16:22.480 --> 16:25.400
Odds are good that
person would be the culprit.

16:26.020 --> 16:30.650
Why not check Sonico's
phone log and text history?

16:30.990 --> 16:34.120
Ena! Now THAT'S how
a great detective thinks!

16:39.370 --> 16:42.479
Sorry to invade your privacy, Sonico!

16:42.480 --> 16:50.480
This is pretty sudden, but today
the owner of Super Nova, where Suzu
works part time, was kind enough to
let us rehearse there after hours.

16:46.690 --> 16:48.249
This is pretty sudden, but today the owner
of SuperNova, where Suzu works part time,

16:48.250 --> 16:51.670
was kind enough to let us
rehearse there after hours.

16:52.510 --> 16:55.140
She... She posted it!

16:55.930 --> 16:58.140
We can't use this to
narrow down the culprit.

16:58.470 --> 17:01.429
Shouldn't we call the police now?

17:01.430 --> 17:04.519
B-but we haven't proven
a crime was committed!

17:04.520 --> 17:08.020
Still, it's a fact that
Nico's guitar is missing.

17:11.190 --> 17:14.819
Nico! Wake up, already! Wake up, Nico!

17:14.820 --> 17:17.119
Suzu, don't be so rough.

17:17.120 --> 17:21.199
She's right, Suzu. If you
wake her, she'll solve the case!

17:21.200 --> 17:23.210
I WANT her to solve the case!

17:23.370 --> 17:25.170
You can trust my theories.

17:25.370 --> 17:27.419
Then tell us who did it, right now!

17:27.420 --> 17:31.170
Um, the culprit was... an alien.

17:31.340 --> 17:33.920
Wake up! Wake up, Nico!

17:35.340 --> 17:36.970
S-Suzu...

17:37.090 --> 17:43.350
Nico! Why did you fall? Where's
your guitar? Was someone in here?!

17:44.060 --> 17:45.850
E-Ena...

17:46.900 --> 17:49.230
N-no! It wasn't me!

17:49.770 --> 17:51.859
Except you came to SuperNova for no reason.

17:51.860 --> 17:54.700
That's because I smelled a case!

17:54.900 --> 17:58.239
Ever since you've shown up, you've said
the waiting room has been locked.

17:58.240 --> 18:00.329
I was e-eavesdropping in the hallway.

18:00.330 --> 18:05.579
Hey... Don't tell me you've been pretending
to be a detective when YOU'RE the culprit...

18:05.580 --> 18:07.920
That it was all a smokescreen!

18:08.170 --> 18:15.220
No, no way! First off, how could I be the culprit
when I have no motive for stealing Sonico's guitar?

18:15.420 --> 18:16.879
No, you do.

18:16.880 --> 18:17.880
Huh?

18:18.680 --> 18:24.310
You call yourself a great detective, and have
wanted to show off your deductive powers to others.

18:24.640 --> 18:32.640
But crimes don't just happen every day.
So you MADE one happen...

18:32.780 --> 18:34.440
E-Ena...

18:34.990 --> 18:36.569
See? Even Nico says so.

18:36.570 --> 18:38.779
She's barely half-awake!

18:38.780 --> 18:43.660
Then prove to us you aren't
the culprit! Go ahead, Ena!

18:43.910 --> 18:46.460
Is this the truth, Ena?

18:46.790 --> 18:49.040
If so, you would be horrible.

18:49.210 --> 18:50.789
You'd be a total criminal!

18:50.790 --> 18:52.340
I'm telling you, you're wrong!

18:54.630 --> 18:56.010
What are you looking at?!

18:58.180 --> 19:01.010
The culprit is... Uh, the culprit...

19:02.350 --> 19:03.509
She ran for it!

19:03.510 --> 19:04.510
Follow her!

19:13.270 --> 19:14.440
Just admit it!

19:17.030 --> 19:19.570
That's... Nico's guitar!

19:20.410 --> 19:22.620
She left it on the stage?

19:23.030 --> 19:24.329
So then, Nico...

19:24.330 --> 19:26.700
She must have just slipped.

19:27.120 --> 19:28.000
No way...

19:28.001 --> 19:30.920
Yes. That is the truth of this case.

19:31.380 --> 19:33.500
I thought the guitar would be here.

19:33.670 --> 19:35.630
It's just as I deduced!

19:36.010 --> 19:38.469
That was just a lucky guess.
It was pure luck.

19:38.470 --> 19:41.050
If you knew that, you should've said so!

20:04.200 --> 20:06.410
Kanashii koto dake ga
There's no way I could disturb

20:08.410 --> 20:11.290
Kimi no mune no uchi o
The sad things

20:08.580 --> 20:11.890
Suzu, what's Nico
doing on the screen?

20:11.980 --> 20:13.845
This is a 3D scan of Nico!

20:13.846 --> 20:15.750
Kakimidasu wake ja nai
Inside your heart

20:15.751 --> 20:17.980
Look, it's creating the
component parts of the model!

20:16.460 --> 20:18.870
Sekai wa nazo darake
The world is full of mysteries

20:18.871 --> 20:20.740
They somehow remind
me of delicious sweets~

20:20.820 --> 20:23.780
No, bad Fuuri.
Oh, it's printing the face now!

20:20.970 --> 20:23.470
Nani ga hontou de atte
What is truth

20:25.140 --> 20:27.850
Nani ga uso da toshite
And what is a lie

20:25.370 --> 20:28.490
This is such a cool machine!
My stomach is empty...

20:28.580 --> 20:31.540
It's called a 3D Printer!
And, you need to be patient, like Nico!

20:29.230 --> 20:31.925
Kitto soko ni kagi wa aru tte
There must surely be a key to that

20:31.926 --> 20:34.120
Oh, it's morning!
Time for breakfast...

20:34.121 --> 20:36.270
Sou, zutto shinjitte kita
Yes Ifve always believed so

20:34.210 --> 20:36.750
Fuuri, you know these pieces
are inedible, right?

20:36.840 --> 20:39.360
I understand.
They just look tasty...

20:39.361 --> 20:41.200
Guuzen, hitsuzen furimaite
A deep mystery

20:39.420 --> 20:41.995
All the pieces are done!
Next it's time to polish them!

20:41.996 --> 20:44.820
Fukamatta MYSTERY
Entrenched in coincidence and inevitability

20:44.821 --> 20:46.130
Ah~ they're so smooth now~

20:46.131 --> 20:49.410
Yokisenu chikara okosu no wa
What awakens that unexpected power

20:47.050 --> 20:49.720
Now to even out rough patches.
Ooh, it feels so nice...

20:49.810 --> 20:52.350
Time to stop the sanding
and finally add color!

20:50.200 --> 20:54.559
Mirai tsukuru bokura sa!
Is US, the ones who build the future!

20:52.480 --> 20:54.480
Wow! Time really flies!
I want to see it in color~

20:54.560 --> 20:56.690
It went by fast since you weren't
waiting for food. It's finally done!

20:56.691 --> 21:00.130
Kore kara zutto tomoshite yukou yo
Now and forever, let's illuminate it

21:00.420 --> 21:04.340
Shinjitsu to iu hikari
That truth called "light"

21:04.760 --> 21:08.510
Sorezore no mune ni yakusoku shiyou yo Let's
promise to keep it inside of every heart

21:08.970 --> 21:10.770
Bokura no akashi Our proof

21:10.980 --> 21:12.270
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa

21:12.430 --> 21:13.850
Don't you forget

21:16.400 --> 21:17.900
Suzu. Fuuri...

21:18.360 --> 21:22.069
I'm really sorry we didn't get to rehearse.

21:22.070 --> 21:25.160
It couldn't be helped. It was an accident.

21:25.860 --> 21:29.030
So, Nico, why did you
lock the waiting room door?

21:29.870 --> 21:33.459
Lock it? No, I didn't lock it.

21:33.460 --> 21:35.419
Huh? Then, why...?

21:35.420 --> 21:38.749
You should hurry.
The last train will leave.

21:38.750 --> 21:43.420
Oh, you're right! Well, Fuuri,
Suzu... See you next time!

21:47.430 --> 21:50.470
The waiting room door was never locked.

21:53.810 --> 21:59.230
That was just an act to make
everyone THINK it was locked.

21:59.980 --> 22:04.610
Quite simple... As simple as your motive.

22:04.860 --> 22:08.740
You couldn't let Sonico and
the others rehearse tonight.

22:09.030 --> 22:13.790
If they had, it would have become clear
that the onstage amp was broken.

22:15.870 --> 22:20.750
Did you not notice the power was on when you
were cleaning? Then spilled some water on it?

22:21.750 --> 22:26.470
I-I was going to tell the owner. But...!

22:27.470 --> 22:32.100
When you saw Sonico passed out in the
waiting room, you decided to take her guitar.

22:32.720 --> 22:37.480
If they didn't know WHEN the amp was broken,
it would make it hard to find out who did it.

22:38.440 --> 22:42.690
I'm sorry! I was scared that I'd be fired!

22:43.820 --> 22:46.820
I thought I'd call someone tomorrow,
secretly have it fixed.

22:47.200 --> 22:51.910
But when I heard Suzu and the others
would use the stage, I panicked!

22:52.410 --> 22:53.410
I...

22:55.040 --> 22:57.620
Relax. I won't tell anyone.

22:57.790 --> 22:58.790
Huh?

22:59.080 --> 23:05.460
Detectives aren't out to catch culprits.
They want to shine light on mysteries...

23:06.470 --> 23:08.930
the light called "truth."

23:12.220 --> 23:18.100
I had to feed them ridiculous theories to delay
rehearsal till it was almost time for the last train...

23:20.000 --> 23:22.859
THE SUPER SONICO MURDER MYSTERY

23:22.860 --> 23:24.940
And it was really hard!

23:25.000 --> 23:33.000
Next Episode Preview

23:25.480 --> 23:28.239
Fuuri, I hear Nico's
university is having a festival!

23:28.240 --> 23:30.819
Oh! It'll be crammed with food stands!

23:30.820 --> 23:35.330
Look! Nico's gonna cosplay, help out
with band, and be in a beauty contest!

23:35.490 --> 23:36.929
That's a lot!

23:36.930 --> 23:40.020
Sonico's Longest Day

23:37.330 --> 23:39.620
Next time, "Sonico's Longest Day."
